{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Connect lan-a and lan-b through a routed WireGuard tunnel using wg01 on node1 and node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both gateways show active wg01 interfaces, reciprocal peer configuration, recent handshakes and traffic counters, tunnel-address reachability, and remote-LAN routes through wg01. The LAN hosts also select their respective VyOS gateways for cross-LAN traffic.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ca97584b3d8d46c4","cmd-048d716129564386","cmd-04c3f9c176464b5f","cmd-1e9b7dfc508d4212","cmd-c13ce0bccfe146ba","cmd-020ce274e5904453"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep routed cross-LAN traffic free of address translation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both gateways report no source or destination NAT configuration, while node3 records node4's original 10.20.20.10 source address for successful requests.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0534ed82a9cc4930","cmd-b505d2ff6ccb4022","cmd-c5dc300f4ada4094"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Serve the lan-a application from node3 on TCP port 8080 and allow node4 to reach it through the tunnel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The application service is enabled, active, and listening on 10.10.10.10:8080. A final request from node4 returned HTTP 200, and node3 logged it from node4's LAN address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ddf6a769a8824af9","cmd-14fc00a1e0c4440a","cmd-c5dc300f4ada4094"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Limit new cross-LAN connections to the node4-to-node3 TCP/8080 application path.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both active forwarding filters default-drop traffic, accept established/related flows, and have a single NEW-flow exception matching node4 to node3 TCP/8080 on the required interfaces. SSH was confirmed listening on both hosts, cross-LAN TCP/22 attempts timed out in both directions, and the gateways' drop counters increased.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3d2225d32f984f05","cmd-7623b1611b844c7d","cmd-0129c85d8e35497f","cmd-1539418646f94a61","cmd-6f646b1009a64e24","cmd-16075a403a114cff","cmd-04c3f9c176464b5f","cmd-1e9b7dfc508d4212"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"No failed services or package inconsistency appeared after execution, and the added WireGuard and application listeners are task-required. A minor deduction applies because systemd explicitly warned that configuring the application under the shared special user nobody is unsafe.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","cmd-fecf7cade10d4325"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied: the LANs are routed through active wg01 peers, the application works end to end without NAT, and stateful default-drop policy restricts new cross-LAN connections to the required application tuple.","limitations":["No reboot or service-restart test was captured, so persistence is supported by saved and enabled configuration but was not behaviorally demonstrated.","Denied traffic was behaviorally sampled with TCP/22 rather than an exhaustive protocol and port scan; the active exact-match, default-drop rules provide the broader policy evidence."]}
